event: response.function_call_arguments.done
data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":762,"item_id":"fc_0fa79c5e89dc7b1e016adb3e4fced0819193e44db281672ccc","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"base_candidate\":3,\"patches\":[{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/4/text\",\"value\":\"For each 0<=r<=lambda<p, r! is invertible modulo p, so X_r and Y_r on the reduced module are the respective nonzero scalar multiples 1/r! of x^r and y^r; for r=0 the scalar is 1. The matrix-unit identities from S002 persist after reduction: their coefficients binom(lambda,j) are nonzero modulo p, and the same identities hold as operators on the K-basis b_0,...,b_lambda corresponding to the characteristic-zero e-basis. Thus any K-subspace W invariant under x and y is invariant under every E_i,j. Let W be arbitrary. If W=0, it is the zero subspace. For the other case, temporarily assume L1: W is nonzero. By the definition of nonzero subspace, there exists a vector w0 in W with w0 nonzero; record this existence before selecting w0 in S006.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/5/text\",\"value\":\"By existential elimination applied to the existence fact F002, choose a witness w0 in W with w0 nonzero; its private identity is used only in this branch. Since b_0,...,b_lambda were established in S004 as a K-basis of M tensor_Z K, there are unique scalars c_i in K with w0=sum_i c_i b_i. At least one coefficient is nonzero, since if all c_i were zero the displayed expansion would give w0=0, contrary to the witness property. Choose an index i in the range 0<=i<=lambda with c_i nonzero; establish this existential fact before selecting i.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/6/text\",\"value\":\"By existential elimination from F003 choose such an index i. For every j with 0<=j<=lambda, matrix-unit action gives E_j,i w0=c_i b_j. Because W is invariant under x and y it is invariant under E_j,i, so E_j,i w0 lies in W. The scalar c_i is nonzero in the field K and hence invertible; since W is a K-subspace, b_j=c_i^{-1}E_j,i w0 lies in W. This holds for each basis vector b_j, so W is the whole module. The chosen w0 and i are used only under L1.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/4/produces/0/statement\",\"value\":\"There exists w0 in W such that w0 is nonzero.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/4/produces/0/binders/0/symbol\",\"value\":\"w0\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/41/symbol\",\"value\":\"w0\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/41/declaration\",\"value\":\"Choose w0 in W with w0 nonzero using the earlier local existence fact F002.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/42/declaration\",\"value\":\"Define the unique coordinates c_i in K by the expansion of the selected vector w0 in the established K-basis b_0,...,b_lambda.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/42/objects/0\",\"value\":\"w0\"}]}}"}

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":763,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0fa79c5e89dc7b1e016adb3e4fced0819193e44db281672ccc","call_id":"call_91010313d8014445a1680d8f567ea684","name":"check_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"base_candidate\":3,\"patches\":[{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/4/text\",\"value\":\"For each 0<=r<=lambda<p, r! is invertible modulo p, so X_r and Y_r on the reduced module are the respective nonzero scalar multiples 1/r! of x^r and y^r; for r=0 the scalar is 1. The matrix-unit identities from S002 persist after reduction: their coefficients binom(lambda,j) are nonzero modulo p, and the same identities hold as operators on the K-basis b_0,...,b_lambda corresponding to the characteristic-zero e-basis. Thus any K-subspace W invariant under x and y is invariant under every E_i,j. Let W be arbitrary. If W=0, it is the zero subspace. For the other case, temporarily assume L1: W is nonzero. By the definition of nonzero subspace, there exists a vector w0 in W with w0 nonzero; record this existence before selecting w0 in S006.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/5/text\",\"value\":\"By existential elimination applied to the existence fact F002, choose a witness w0 in W with w0 nonzero; its private identity is used only in this branch. Since b_0,...,b_lambda were established in S004 as a K-basis of M tensor_Z K, there are unique scalars c_i in K with w0=sum_i c_i b_i. At least one coefficient is nonzero, since if all c_i were zero the displayed expansion would give w0=0, contrary to the witness property. Choose an index i in the range 0<=i<=lambda with c_i nonzero; establish this existential fact before selecting i.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/6/text\",\"value\":\"By existential elimination from F003 choose such an index i. For every j with 0<=j<=lambda, matrix-unit action gives E_j,i w0=c_i b_j. Because W is invariant under x and y it is invariant under E_j,i, so E_j,i w0 lies in W. The scalar c_i is nonzero in the field K and hence invertible; since W is a K-subspace, b_j=c_i^{-1}E_j,i w0 lies in W. This holds for each basis vector b_j, so W is the whole module. The chosen w0 and i are used only under L1.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/4/produces/0/statement\",\"value\":\"There exists w0 in W such that w0 is nonzero.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/4/produces/0/binders/0/symbol\",\"value\":\"w0\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/41/symbol\",\"value\":\"w0\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/41/declaration\",\"value\":\"Choose w0 in W with w0 nonzero using the earlier local existence fact F002.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/42/declaration\",\"value\":\"Define the unique coordinates c_i in K by the expansion of the selected vector w0 in the established K-basis b_0,...,b_lambda.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/42/objects/0\",\"value\":\"w0\"}]}}","status":"completed"}}

