tRZe4XfH2G6c6-zdXGI_Z-e6XrhTKg=="},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0fa79c5e89dc7b1e016adb3e4fced0819193e44db281672ccc","call_id":"call_91010313d8014445a1680d8f567ea684","name":"check_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"base_candidate\":3,\"patches\":[{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/4/text\",\"value\":\"For each 0<=r<=lambda<p, r! is invertible modulo p, so X_r and Y_r on the reduced module are the respective nonzero scalar multiples 1/r! of x^r and y^r; for r=0 the scalar is 1. The matrix-unit identities from S002 persist after reduction: their coefficients binom(lambda,j) are nonzero modulo p, and the same identities hold as operators on the K-basis b_0,...,b_lambda corresponding to the characteristic-zero e-basis. Thus any K-subspace W invariant under x and y is invariant under every E_i,j. Let W be arbitrary. If W=0, it is the zero subspace. For the other case, temporarily assume L1: W is nonzero. By the definition of nonzero subspace, there exists a vector w0 in W with w0 nonzero; record this existence before selecting w0 in S006.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/5/text\",\"value\":\"By existential elimination applied to the existence fact F002, choose a witness w0 in W with w0 nonzero; its private identity is used only in this branch. Since b_0,...,b_lambda were established in S004 as a K-basis of M tensor_Z K, there are unique scalars c_i in K with w0=sum_i c_i b_i. At least one coefficient is nonzero, since if all c_i were zero the displayed expansion would give w0=0, contrary to the witness property. Choose an index i in the range 0<=i<=lambda with c_i nonzero; establish this existential fact before selecting i.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/6/text\",\"value\":\"By existential elimination from F003 choose such an index i. For every j with 0<=j<=lambda, matrix-unit action gives E_j,i w0=c_i b_j. Because W is invariant under x and y it is invariant under E_j,i, so E_j,i w0 lies in W. The scalar c_i is nonzero in the field K and hence invertible; since W is a K-subspace, b_j=c_i^{-1}E_j,i w0 lies in W. This holds for each basis vector b_j, so W is the whole module. The chosen w0 and i are used only under L1.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/4/produces/0/statement\",\"value\":\"There exists w0 in W such that w0 is nonzero.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/4/produces/0/binders/0/symbol\",\"value\":\"w0\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/41/symbol\",\"value\":\"w0\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/41/declaration\",\"value\":\"Choose w0 in W with w0 nonzero using the earlier local existence fact F002.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/42/declaration\",\"value\":\"Define the unique coordinates c_i in K by the expansion of the selected vector w0 in the established K-basis b_0,...,b_lambda.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/42/objects/0\",\"value\":\"w0\"}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report exact status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP or SUSPECTED_GAP stops for an actual unsupported mathematical implication; give its premises, conclusion and mathematical grounds. SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT stops for a real source-access/original-input obstacle. Ordinary unfinished drafting, source registration or format work must use TASK_INCOMPLETE: this records progress without ending the stage; continue the actual work. Difficulty or artifact incompletion alone is not a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"obstacle_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["obstacle_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an act